Endesa and Barcelona by electric car
The electricity company Endesa, together with the city of Barcelona, has created the "LIVE office".
This is a project for the development and promotion of the electric car in the Catalan capital.
The "LIVE office" (logistics on the introduction of the electric car) will define and coordinate the roadmap for the introduction of the electric car in the city and make arrangements regarding mobility by managing, coordinating, subsidizing, etc.
On the other hand, the MOVELE project is currently being developed in order to promote electric cars and to summarize the opinions and measures of the areas involved.
This is an attempt to advance the means of transport of the future.
3 "electrical cities"
Barcelona, however, is not the only city that will be involved in the introduction of the electric car in Spain.
Madrid and Seville are also participating in this project.
These are the three cities chosen by the government in the MOVELE project to accelerate the introduction of the electric car.
The electricity company Endesa has already signed a framework agreement with the government of Catalonia (la Generalitat).
With this framework agreement, one wants to promote the activities of research and technological development in the Autonomous Community of Catalonia.
These activities involve, among other things, those activities related to energy and, in particular, their performance.
However, it is by no means the only initiative in which Endesa participates with a view to the promotion of the electric car.
The company participates in standardization groups throughout Europe and maintains a whole range of additional projects such as G4V, ELVIRE or CENIT VERDE.
Zapatero sees 'a horizon of tranquility' for the automotive sector
The president-of-governmen, José Luis Rodríguez Zapatero, prophesies "a horizon of tranquility" for the Spanish automotive industry, which is the country's largest exporter.
Presenting the economic report for 2009 by the president of the government, Zapatero once again reminded us of the measures that the government initiated in support of the automotive sector over the course of the year.
"Without the plan on the competitiveness of the car industry, today we would have a panorama of neglect and closure of some of our main production plants," he said.
"Thanks to this plan and the willingness of carmakers to continue to produce in Spain in a very competitive sector of industry in the future, we can see a calm horizon for the future of this industry, which is our largest export industry," he added.
He also recalled that the Competitiveness Plan, which is part of the total plan for the automotive industry (PIA), has provided 800 million euros for projects by 19 vehicle manufacturers and 137 suppliers, which in turn ensured investments of more than 3 billion euros.
The head of government stated that these investments are intended both for the development of new models and for the modernization of existing products and processes.
Zapatero also underlined the measures taken by the government to stimulate demand, in reference to Plan 2000E, applied in cooperation with the Autonomous Communities and car manufacturers.
According to the head of government , this plan allows to reduce the exhaust gases in new vehicles sold on the Spanish market by an average of 6%, which in turn led to a "strong increase" in registrations, which increased "by 40 percent" in November.
On 20,000 square meters of classic vehicles
In Madrid, the first edition of the International Classical Automobile Fair is held, an exhibition for professionals and lovers of the world of engines.
This fair will take place from 5 to 7 February 2010 in the Pabellón de Cristal of the Casa de Campo in Madrid.
On an exhibition area of 20,000 square meters, 200 domestic and foreign exhibitors will demonstrate their brands.
You can not only marvel at classic motorcycles and vehicles, but you will also find all imaginable articles in connection with the world of engines at ClassicAuto Madrid.
So you can find accessories, spare parts, components, fabric accessories, accessories, publications, miniature cars, etc.
Hundreds of articles from the world of classic motors, which will inspire the collectors and lovers.
Among the companies who will participate in this trade fair include Clásicos de Mos and Good Old Times, vehicle sales; Juan Lumbreras, restorations; Coupe-Francisco pueche, sales and restoration of automobiles, specializing in Mercedes Benz.
Skilfulness tests in the outdoor area
In addition, the sales activities at this fair are supplemented by parallel events: meetings, sports vehicle exhibitions, skill tests, events and competitions.
Skill tests with classic cars and motorcycles are also carried out on a specially designed race track in the outdoor area of the exhibition grounds.
Mazda3 i-Stop: Environmentally friendly sportsmanship
Mazda wants to prove that sportsmanship is quite compatible with the protection of the environment.
For this reason, Mazda has recently introduced the automatic stop and start-up system of the engine, christened i-Stop, the Mazda, a device that is currently only available for the 2.0 gasoline engine with 150 hp.
This second generation of Mazdas 3 stands out with its good grades in the overall picture.
The final processing, the execution of the vehicle, the comfort, its routing behavior, the mechanics, the i-stop system ...
All these aspects are "very good" with the new Mazda3.
Starting with the front seats, it can be seen that the front seats offer excellent ergonomics and good support.
Furthermore, the game of the steering wheel is excellent.
When looking further at the unit, which consists of the instrument panel and the dashboard, it can be noted that Mazda with a variety of buttons and switches in the eye-catching colors red and blue, on the same line as the Japanese trend towards a futuristic interior design.
This style partly reminds us of the style of the Honda Civics.
Therefore, it can easily be said that both the Mazda 3, as well as the Civic, both Japanese models, stand out from the sobriety of German automobiles, especially from the Volkswagen Golf, which everyone wants to surpass.
The passenger compartment of these two Japanese compact cars offers more than ever the appropriate comfort, so that four adults can travel comfortably by car.
To all this comes a spacious and clearly shaped trunk.
Until now, the stopping and starting system is only available for the 2-liter petrol engine with 150 hp and a 6-speed shift.
This engine is a real pleasure. It stands out through its subtlety, due to its quiet noises, its performances and its low consumption.
And all those who don’t drive many kilometers a year should consider this i-stop with a gasoline engine because of its great comfort in gear shifting and its low consumption, even if Mazda’s diesel models are the best-selling.
In terms of the equipment, the so-called Sportive model selected for the test drive is a special feature, since it has a much larger number of elements from the standard equipment.
Above all, the assistant for the lane change (RVM) stands out from the production equipment, which thus abolishes the blind spot, but also the controls for traction and stability, the speed control, the light-sensitive interior mirror, the on-board computer with a large screen, the sensors for parking, independent air conditioning, raining and light sensors, Bluetooth and audio bluetooth as well as
In addition, this version also includes, as if that would not be enough equipment, the Premium package, which for an additional 1,500 euros contains the following: in addition to other elements, especially the learnable Bixenon headlights and the sound system BOSE with CD charger.
Conclusion
The Mazda3 2.0 i-Stop is one of the best compact cars in its class.
It is particularly outstanding with regard to the materials used, because of its driving behavior and the variety of equipment.
In addition, those who don’t cover many kilometers a year can also buy the i-stop version, which is only available with a 2.0 gasoline engine with 150 hp.
The only negative thing about this model is its slightly high price, which is between 21,770 euros for the Luxury model and 23,270 euros for the rehearsal model Sportive.
In return at this high price, however, the Mazda3 offers us the highest pass every day.
