Manuel Vicent's poker game
Manuel Vicent presents in "Poker der Asse" (Alfaguara, illustrations by Fernando Vicente) to the three-minute X-rays of writers who have accompanied him in his literary life (and, in some cases, even in real life).
He does not use a predictable and terrifying genre (short biography, life and work), but is looking for a similarity to the fervent centerpiece of the Creator.
The journey is exciting and Vicent doesn’t save on horrors or enlightenments.
Excluding that this book is a delicious reading pleasure, it is also a moving invitation to read and reading again and again.
Here are a few excerpts from the book.
About Albert Camus: "When reading his pages, I found out that the Mediterranean is not a sea, but rather a spiritual, almost sensuous instinct, just as I have always felt, without having found words for it: the joy in opposition to ominous fate, morality without guilt and innocence without any God."
About Samuel Beckett: "Nihilist, allegorical Christian, he wrote about what he had in blood, not in his mind, between impotence and ignorance, with a stunning poetic humour, without any meaning, like the knife blade that almost killed him."
"Our man was captivated by this woman with a passion that lasted for thirteen years, in whose flesh the emotions united with the pleasure of remorse due to adultery, a spiritual privilege that consisted in coming to heaven on the detour of perdition."
About James Joyce: "The Odysseus" was edited by Sylvia Beach in 1922 in Paris. This is one of the 8000 peaks in worldwide literature, you have to climb up on the north wall, on the wall, where the best mountaineers try again and again."
William Faulkner: "He was a weird owl.
He sometimes said about himself that he was the heir of a county's landowner and again other times he said that he was the son of a black man and a crocodile.
Both dreams testified to a certain size.”
About Louis-Ferdinand Céline: This writer recorded the insane cry that was shouted out from a bridge by that personality from Munich, so that his echo reverberated in his literary way deep into the night of the 20th century. He did this on a journey on which he fled from himself and begged posterity with a speech full of violence from the worms.
About Dorothy Parker: "One day she knelted and begged, “My revered God, I ask you to do everything in your power so that I can finally stop writing like a woman.”
About Joseph Conrad: "On his tomb these verses are engraved by Spencer: 'sleep after the exertion, / after the thunderstorm of the harbor, / the rest after the war, / after a rich life you find pleasure in death."
About Virginia Wolf: "In her luggage she also always had her depression with her.
Husband took it with complete normalcy when she told him that Edward VII was spying on between the azaleas or the birds singing in Greek.
Not a single other case is known where the man had so much patience and was in love with a neurotician whose literary talent was much greater than her craziness.”
About Pío Baroja: "What else did Martín-Santos do than trying to influte Joyce into Baroja?
What did Benet intend to do if he didn't introduce Baroiah to Faulkner's weapons?
What did Cela do to destroy the glory of that man, so that he could put himself on this podium?
Cowardly aggression
My 70-year-old mother was walking through our district in the village of Fuenlabrada last week, when suddenly a group of young people between the ages of 15 and 18 ran next to her and our dog, our dog is a mongrel, whom we brought from the shelter and which weighs just six kilos, and then out of the sky they gave him two footsteps and seriously injured him.
Our indignation cannot be put into words, since it is incomprehensible to us, where there should be fun with a cheap aggression against a small and helpless animal, which was of course carried out on a leash.
In addition, there is the suffocacy that a woman who walked comfortably when she wanted to rebuke these people due to the incident, she even feared for her own life, because if such a manager attacks a dog, he may also do the same with a woman, a child, an older gentleman or probably with anyone who is weaker than himself.
The incident took place in a normally quiet neighborhood at five o'clock in the afternoon on an ordinary Tuesday.
The dog has been howling all day.
Of course, we have filed a complaint in a nearby police station, but we have great doubts whether this will bring anything at all and in order to prevent possible prejudices from the outset, we only want to make it clear that the cowardly criminals were Spaniards.
Our indignation of what happened prompted us to report this incident.
We can’t understand what needs to be in the minds of these young people, that they’re making a cheap attack on a helpless animal funny, to an animal that gives us love, society, and friendship.
We don't know where good education and respect for the animals and the individuals have remained.
Michelin and Fesvial together for the use of the helmet
In cooperation with the Spanish Foundation for Road Safety (Fesvial), the tyre manufacturer Michelin has launched a campaign to promote helmet use, especially among younger motorcyclists, both companies announced today.
This initiative aims to draw attention to the importance of helmet use, since this is ultimately the only protective element that can prevent head injuries or even death in the event of a motorcycle accident.
Michelin pointed out that this campaign represents part of its commitment to road safety, which "consisters far more than the designing and manufacturing of products that are getting safer and safer every day" and further reaffirmed that, even with other actions of educational and informative character, they contribute to getting one step closer to this goal every day.
This new campaign to promote the use of helmets on the motorcycle, which runs under the slogan 'To be or not to be', will distribute posters to over 500 motorcycle workshops in a first phase in order to achieve the best possible proliferation.
Finally, Michelin emphasized that road safety is "a constant concern" of the company, and precisely because, as a manufacturer of tires for two-wheeled vehicles, she is always committed to that one of her main objectives must be the development of increasingly safer products.
The sale of small trucks is rising again somewhat
After almost two years, the car market for vans is finally beginning to see some light at the end of the dark tunnel.
The 9,425 vehicles registered in Spain in November represent an increase of 12.6% in relation to 2008, and, more importantly, they are thus the first increase ever after 22 consecutive months with a steady decline, according to the figures presented by the manufacturing association Anfac and the car dealer association Ganvam.
However, these good figures are currently only possible with great caution, as the reference data used for the comparison are from November 2008, which was a particularly poor financial year with a decrease of 60% in respect of the previous year.
However, it must be borne in mind that, apart from the increase last month, the total approvals of these 11 months are still 40% below the sales figures of the previous financial year.
Since January, a total of 95,853 vehicles have been sold, but this number includes all vehicles that make up the van market: descendants of passenger cars, pick-ups, vans, small vans and lighter small trucks/companies.
Furthermore, there are still the same thunderclouds in the skies, which most affect the demand, because even if some of the vehicles are purchased by private individuals, the majority of sales go to small and medium-sized enterprises, which make the purchase with third-party financing in almost 100% of all cases.
For example, one has to include other factors for these restrictions, which are the result of the turned-over money tap of the credit institutions, such as the increase in the unemployment rate or the persistence of the bad economic situation.
With this panorama and in contrast to the passenger cars, the financial supports in the purchase of a vehicle of the Plan 2000E did little to help.
However, this plan is not only intended for private individuals, self-employed and small companies also have a right if they want to buy a van up to 3.5 tons with a CO2 emission, which may not exceed 160 grams per kilometer driven, but the low sales figures speak for themselves.
Especially yesterday Ganvam had reminded that it is absolutely necessary by the state to pay special attention to these small trucks as well as, of course, to the industrial vehicles (lorries and buses).
For the year 2010, the car dealer association predicted a similar year as the previous year, for which it expects a loss of sales (in the case of passenger cars and SUVs) of 19%.
Assistance with braking maneuvers in critical situations is now mandatory
As with the anti-lock braking system ABS at that time and as happens now with the stability control ESP, the auxiliary systems for braking in emergencies have to become compulsory equipment in European cars.
In fact, they are obligatory for all newly registered passenger cars and light vans, for the remaining vehicles a waiting period until the end of February 2011 has been fixed.
The measure adopted by the European Union aims to improve the protection of pedestrians, but these braking systems can also help to prevent many rear-end collisions due to their operation.
The task of the emergency brake assistant is to exert more pressure on the brakes in the case of a critical braking manoeuvre, which recognizes the system based on the braking strength to the brake pedal executed by the driver.
However, this system does not exert this pressure until the end.
According to an investigation commissioned by the component manufacturer for the Bosch vehicles, a third of the drivers involved in an accident could no longer come to step onto the brake pedal and half of them had not braked with full force.
Up to 1,100 Accidents
The braking aid, on the other hand, engages in the braking system with maximum force and thereby reduces the braking time and thus also the braking distance that a car travels during the braking process.
According to an EU study, up to 1,100 deadly accidents involving pedestrians could be prevented every year if all cars were equipped with this type of emergency braking assistant.
There would be even fewer accidents - it is expected that every fourth accident with personal injury could be prevented - once the so-called intelligent emergency braking systems become popular.
Then the vehicle is equipped with a system that detects obstacles (via radar or a camera) and warns the driver, whereby at the same time it exerts a slight pressure on the brakes.
If the driver reacts, the system helps him to increase the pressure on the brake pedal if it becomes necessary.
If the driver does not respond to the warning and even if the collision is already unavoidable, the brake assistant exerts maximum pressure on the brakes in order to keep the damage as low as possible.
General Motors postpones plan for Opel until January
While the Opel plant’s workforce in Figueruelas (Zaragoza) has already been briefed by Nick Reilly, the new chairman of General Motors (GM) Europe, that production of the new Meriva will start in the first week of April, probably on April 8, according to Javier Ortega, the American vehicle manufacturer points out that he needs more time to finalize the rescue plan for Opel.
Nick Reilly, the new chairman of GM Europa, wants to ensure that the affected side gives their consent to every single point of the plan in advance.
And for this reason it may be possible that the final document, which will be submitted first to the workers and then to the governments of the lands in which there are works, will be postponed until the beginning of 2010.
On the other hand, GM is assured that it will make a decision regarding the sale of Saab in the next few days.
So it is not surprising that the Swedish government has increased the pressure on the American car manufacturer so that it makes a decision as soon as possible.
GM admits to being in contact with some possible new buyers.
One of these buyers could be Geely, who would also like to buy Volvo, but the option of the Dutch manufacturer of Skyper sports cars, which is backed by the Russian group Converg, is becoming increasingly popular.
If none of these buyers were to reach an agreement, GM could sell some assets to China's BAIC.
The decision to close Saab at the end of the year, if it has not been sold by then, will continue to be maintained.
At the wheel of Porsche Boxster Spyder
For the development of their latest and very expensive jewel, the engineers used the Boxster S as the basis and really managed to make it lighter by 80 kilos, with which he now weighs only 1,275 kilos.
In order to create such a thing, they first dispensed with the automatic folding roof, which was replaced by a tent canopy roof with a manual drive, so that 21 kilos have been saved; thanks to the aluminum doors used in this model, such as those of the GT3 "disappear" another 15; with the removal of the air conditioning again 13; in addition, the fuel tank has been reduced from 64 to 54 liters
Then you had reached another six kilos less by dispensing with the audio system CDR-30 and the missing kilo by replacing the door handles with handles made of fabric.
Even though it is also available with the PDK dual-clutch transmission, the test drive was carried out with a vehicle with a 6-speed manual transmission, mainly on the smaller highways of California, on mountain routes that were really very curvy.
In his driving behavior you can only give him the grade impeccable.
However, the reduction in his weight has by no means meant that he would no longer be so safe on the road.
It’s rather the oppose: for a long time, we haven’t tested such a small and light model, which at the same time also gives you a feeling of great safety in the curves, even at high speed.
He is a small athlete, able to warm his muscles at a low gear in the required time, until we give him the orders to race, brake, recover and then get everything out of his engine again ...
He does everything he's told. The car does everything we hint at him with our hands on the steering wheel, thanks to his steering, which is as communicative as it is precise.
And he's doing it with a surgeon's precision.
An engine sound for all flavors
The sound of its V6 boxer with 320 hp (10 more than the Boxster S) has been extremely successful and you can increase it with the 'sport' option as well as with a system that can change the engine noise, which was already used for the first time at Panamera.
Accelerability is unimaginably brutal, regardless of whether it’s standing out or accelerating again.
The suspensions are strong, but not hard or uncomfortable.
The tarmac on the country roads, on which we drove with the Boxster Spyder, was already quite damaged, but the car mastered the potholes well.
The electronic assistants had almost nothing to do on the entire track; and that's even though we found ice at dawn at dawn and roll split in the morning during some of these curves.
In summary, you can say that it is an ultralight car, a car with which you have an indescribable lane pass, as it arguably rarely exists and in it there is much more than just a small improvement of the Boxster Ss.
The car will be on the market in February 2010 and will cost 70,831 EURos.
Bag Girl'
The singer, a bosom friend by Karl Lagerfeld, is the face of the Coco Cocoon cosmetics line and an occasional starlet at the fashion shows of 'maison', she presents her nasty face with the same stiff-neckedness as her pockets of Chanel.
Much more than "Bad Girl" or "It Girl," she's a "Bag Girl."
Baskonia gives itself a victory in Israel
The Caja Laboral, despite the many unusual players in Dusko Ivanovic's squad, celebrated an excellent triumph with 82-91 on his visit on the complicated football field of Maccabi Electra and thus comes to the first place within his group after the great performance of Mirza Teletovic, who was the best of his squad with eight triples (29 in the rating).
The team from Vitoria was able to replace the significant failures of Herrmann, Oleson, Huertas or Micov with a large dose of commitment and teamwork, even if they had to wait until the bitter end for their victory.
The great hits from the perimeter with 16 rated triples contributed significantly to their final victory.
The game began with the leadership of the Blue Reds, who sat down at the top of the scoreboard right from the start.
Since the first four baskets of the team from Vitoria already came out of the perimeter, you could already guess that they had come onto the field with well-warmed wrists.
It was English and Teletovic who were mainly responsible for the 18-20 at the end of the first quarter.
The second quarter was hardly different, only that the team from Álava opted for an internal game of Barac and for the game of Eliyahu, who was received on his return to the squad with whistles and applause, which is his home to further expand their advantage until the break (34-43).
Teletovic has already begun to stand out as the best of his squad with 13 points, even though the "minus six" rating from Splitter already suggests that this would not be the Brazilian's best evening.
Nevertheless, despite the clear advantage at the break, the game was far from decided and the Maccabees wanted to remind the Vitorians once again that not everyone wins on their field, and thanks to the repeatedly attacking "hand of Elías" they came back into the game.
Eidson and Pnini contributed decisively to the "yellows" turning the rudder (50-49).
Even more disadvantages
Ivanovic's team, injured but anything but dead, had to prepare a few moves with accuracy to get air again and with one of them suddenly came the pistol from Mirza Teletovic, who, with three almost consecutive triples and with the support of English and Ribas, made sure that on the scoreboard again reassuring distance of (54-67) was displayed.
The Alaveses were exposed in the last neighborhood and English and San Emeterio (60-75) already announced that they would not allow anyone to take away from them the victory they honestly deserved in the first three minutes.
Nonetheless, Pnini and Eidson resigned the best of their squad and tried to give their squad strength again through three points from the line (70-77).
Nevertheless, and even though splinters were put off because of foul, Ivanovic's team didn't give up, defended well and even though the Israelis were still catching up in the last minute (80-85), the game already had a winner and Tel Aviv lost for the first time this season.
Injuries prevented Unicaja's foreheast
Unicaja lost loudly in Greece against Olympiacos and had to cede the lead in Group B of the Euroliga to him, and that in a game marked by the failures on the part of the players of Unicajas (Freeland, Lima and Archibald), especially at the inner game, which facilitated victory for the Greeks.
The Málaga team was neither afraid of the mood in the hall of peace and friendship nor of the opposing team, which is perhaps one of the strongest in Europe and has a lot of money.
Thanks to their presented game in the first quarters, the Andalusians were allowed to start dreaming. An aggressive defense and three consecutive triples, two of them by Omar Cook and one by Guillem Rubio, dazzled the hosts by 12-18 in the 9th minute.
Olympiacos was surprised by the intensity of Unicaja, even if the local squad with an inner match between Bourousis, Vujcic and Schortsanitis managed to indicate the scoreboard in their favour in the 13th minute 22-20, the minute in which there would have been almost a brawl between the two Americans Beverley and Williams and why both were disqualified.
The Greek team began to finally get warm and its superiority on both halves of the game, while Englishman Joel Freeland's exit due to an injury and Carlos Jiménez's three mistakes caused behind clear marks on Unicaja.
Among their players in the insidion and the Lithuanian foreplayer Linas Kleizas, with his triples, they increased their advantage in the 19th minute to 44-32.
Catch-up was impossible
The third number was characterized by many attacks against Olympiaco's squad, which was superior despite its 19 losses and even managed to make up for the difference of the match played in Malaga with 66-48 in the 27th minute, which in turn fluctuated the lead within the group.
Unicaja tried to override the many failures and the elimination of Scot Robert Archibald, who was injured during the game.
Despite the many drawbacks for the Unicaja in the 31st minute thanks to the lead and the triples of Cook and the use of Lewis, there was some hope of 66-57 again.
Nevertheless, it was actually impossible, as soon as Olympiacos attacked and showed his superiority with centimeters within the basket area could not be braked.
Croatian captain Nikola Vujcic managed in the 37th minute to increase the basket difference to 81-62 and Unicaja had to give himself up beaten and had to cede the lead to Olympiacos.
How much should you earn based on your Facebook profile?
Facebook's users can now know their salary thanks to the new application Trovit, the search engine with most advertisements of real estate, vacancies and cars in Spain, that they should earn because of their profile.
The tool “How much should you earn?” calculates users’ salaries based on more than 140,000 job offers available at Trovit in Spain. Users will have a form available in Facebook where their profession, work experience, age, and the city where they work can enter.
Already after one week after the application was available for the first time, the search engine found that the Spanish worker "feels paid poorly" on average, Albert Ribera, who is responsible for the Trovit product, explains in a press release.
Spaniards are the worst-paid according to the data Trovit has through his search engines in the UK and France.
A British programmer gets an annual gross salary of 45,226 euros and a french person 31,059, in contrast to the 24,000 euros a Spaniard earns.
As a result, a truck driver has an annual net salary of 34,247 euros in England, 25,751 in France and 16,420 euros in Spain.
According to Trovit, the worst-paid work in Spain is that of a waiter with 11,592 euros annually net; followed by the work of a seller with 14,725 euros and that of a worker with 15,667 euros.
The most wanted jobs on the Internet in the last three months are that of a driver, half-day positions and social workers.
Brazil names Zelaya a date to leave
The Brazilian government set a deadline to Manuel Zelaya's stay at her embassy in Tegucigalpa.
The president removed from office must leave diplomatic representation no later than January 27, 2010, when his mandate officially expires
Francisco Catunda, the trade delegate of the Brazilian embassy in the Honduran capital, confirmed to TV Globo that "Mel" knows that before that date he must have left the embassy where he had found asylum since September 21.
"He is aware that he will have to leave on 27 January, as his mandate expires on this day and he will have to look for new accommodation."
The station also quoted the ex-president, who confirmed his intention to leave the embassy ahead of the scheduled date: "My point of view is to leave as soon as possible, logically with the backing of Brazil's government," Zelaya explained on the phone.
After the elections on November 29 (in which Porfirio Lobo emerged victorious), Zelaya assured that he would stay in the Brazilian embassy until January.
However, he tried to get refuge in Brazil this week.
This failed, however, due to Zelaya's refusal to acknowledge the status of an asylum-seeking politician, whom the "de facto" government under the chairmanship of Roberto Micheletti wanted to impose on him.
Thank you very much!
After tempting days since last spring, when the inflation of assets was the predominant mood in the markets, uncertainty has returned in the markets, which is by no means surprising, as this is their natural state, in an environment in which the brokers make decisions about an inherently unsafe future.
The measure used to stabilise the markets was to settle the debt with the direct purchase of assets and to indirectly leave liquidity vacant at interest rates that move around zero, so that in this way the banks buy assets to settle.
The central banks have already confirmed that the direct purchases of assets are almost finished and, without questioning their heterodox policy on liquidity, are beginning to sprinkle some sand into the gears, as the BCE has already pretended with its annual auction taking place next week.
That's why investors doubt the global economy's ability to maintain the economic recovery without these heterodoxic measures and we're just witnessing a reversal in reducing risk premiums.
The fugitivities of the exchanges and the differences in corporate bonuses are rising again, even if they are still a long way from the paranormal amounts they reached at the beginning of the year.
States were compelled to nationalize the private risks and government debtories are rising again.
We are now relying on quality again and the USA, Japan and Germany are the preferred refuge for investors, which in turn leads to an increase in the differences between the countries of the eurozone with regard to Germany.
Spain has hardly been affected by this episode of instability until now, but then Came Standard & Poor's and threatened a new revision downwards regarding Spain's assessment.
On the other hand, a certain degree of insecurity does not hurt to silence the defenders of the moral risk, who had once again tried to raise awareness among those in charge of world economic policy for what they had caused, since they had slowed down the devastating effects of restricting loans to the loss of jobs, when they were actually supposed to decide on a new day.
Nevertheless, what happened in Dubai indicates a tribal war between the Emires in order to restore power in the Emirates and the development in Greece has also been foreseen earlier.
A government that conceals national debt, elections and a new government pulling together in the same direction.
Prodi made it in Italy to Berlusconi and Sócrates in Portugal to Durão Barroso.
It makes no sense that Ecofin save Hungary earlier this year from non-compliance with its foreign payments and thus grants a euro-member country not to meet its obligations anymore.
On the other hand, it is logical that Ecofin forced the Greek government to be transparent and take its citizens into account in order to maintain the stability of state funds.
Yes, as expected, we are ahead of an episode of normalization of risk premiums, after a few debaucheries to excessive amounts, that would now be within what's expected.
In the case of Spain, you don’t have to worry, as long as the differences in public debt increase at the same speed as European corporate bonuses.
However, if the European differences are reduced and the Spanish continue to increase, this would be a special Spanish risk.
That of Standard & Poor's is a farce. While the local early indicators force a majority of market research institutes to bring forward their scenarios for the recovery and to correct their scenario upwards for 2011, including the OCDE and the European Commission, which come again with a Japanese scenario for the Spanish economy, all this does not promise a long lifespan despite warnings.
Once again, it seems that it is an excellent opportunity to buy Spanish stocks, although at the moment "caution when driving" is announced.
Connected branches
Iberdrola's chairman, Ignacio Sánchez Galán, was the first to appear before Parliament's sub-committee yesterday, where Spain's energy supply strategy will be debated these days over the next two decades.
After his appearance, which was followed by the chairman of Gas Natural-Fenosa, Rafael Villaseca, Galán gave the press a few sticking points about what he had submitted to the subcommittee behind closed doors.
According to Iberdrola's chairman, Spain will have to invest 50 billion euros by 2020 and a further 60 billion from this date by 2030, under the condition that the current nuclear power plants continue to operate.
If this is not the case, the necessary investments would not amount to 60 billion, but up to 95 billion.
However, Iberdrola believes that one should no longer invest in an increase in energy generation capacity, but in distribution networks and international alliances.
From 2020, the question will change and one should increase the performance.
His proposal focuses on both gas and coal plants with facilities to collect carbon dioxide and, of course, above all on renewable energies.
In this case, he assumes that 18,000 MW more will be needed, under the prerequisitive nature by other "support energies."
Galán, who thinks that the bill for a sustainable economy that has just been passed by the government is in line with what his company has demanded, by no means wanted to say anything against this law, such as creating incentives for national coal consumption, which would be exactly the opposite of all the political strategies in the fight against climate change.
In his opinion, "in the long term, one relies clearly on this direction, despite some "individual" measures, as the chairman of Iberdrola called it.
Be it as it may, Galán says, that decisions on investment should already be taken now, even if they are long-term, because it will take some time and a stable remuneration framework will have to be created in order to tackle them.
Ferrovial gets the "handling" from Aer Lingus at ten airports
Ferrovial's subsidiary for services at airports on the ground, Swiss-Swiss Swissport, is the preferred partner of Ireland's airline Aer Lingus for luggage service at ten European airports where they are represented.
Paris, London, Frankfurt and Brussels are some of the most important.
The agreement, for which no figures have yet been announced, is planned for five years.
On the other hand, Ferrovial, the government of Castile-La Mancha and the University of Alcalá de Henares yesterday signed a protocol for cooperation to create an innovation center for smart infrastructures.
The alliance is planning investments of 20 million by 2012, of which 50% will come from Ferrovial.
One of the centre's tasks will be an examination of energy efficiency on motorways and airports.
Acciona competes with Hochtief and Bouygues for his first highway construction in Australia
Acciona is campaigning for the approval of its first highway in Australia, a market where they are already represented as energy and water companies.
The building, which is involved, is a tunnel that will cost 1.7 billion Australian dollars (approximately 1.047 billion euros).
The French company Bouygues and the German Hochtief are its competitors.
A 5-kilometre tunnel in the Australian city of Brisbane, on the east coast, has become the best opportunity for Acciona to establish itself as a construction company and highway operator in the country.
The city administration would like to have the construction completed at the end of 2014.
After the administration had opted for public-private cooperation (PPP is the English abbreviation) to advance the project according to a business plan drawn up by Ernst & Young, the administration is already in possession of a definitive list of candidates for construction and toll management.
In anticipation of the offers presented in May, the estimated investments amount to 1.7 billion Australian dollars (1.047 billion euros), with three consortia, mainly consisting of European construction companies, competing with each other in the last phase.
The group called Transcity is led by Acciona, the only Spanish company, and its partners are BMD and Ghella.
The first company is one of Australia's largest construction companies, while the second, based in Italy, is one of the best civil engineering specialists.
Against Acciona's team, the Northern Direct consortium, formed by British company Laing O'Rourke, Australia's Transfield, which is responsible for the infrastructures and France's Bouygues construction group.
The third and final consortium, which is shortlisted, is LBRJV, formed from the capital of the Australian Leighton (subsidiary of the german construction company Hochtief, which in turn belongs to ACS), the likewise native Baulderstone (owned by the german group Bilfinger Berger) and the French company Razel, which specializes in public construction.
The Australian market for infrastructure promises huge construction and privatizations, but has a hurdle that needs to be overcome, as you only gain access through the purchase of a domestic construction company.
A strategy that was followed by those companies Hochtief or Bilfinger, in addition to Asian references, and which has yet to be pursued by the Spanish baugiants.
Even ACS has only gained access to this market through its 30% stake in Hochtief, owner of the aforementioned Leighton.
Millions in assets
Acciona relies on this geographical area of the utmost importance for the industry, in which it is already very well-known due to its activity as an energy supplier and in the desalination industry.
Under further assets, it already has its largest windmill farm (192 MW) in Victoria and leads the group of companies tasked with building and managing Adelaide's desalination plant with a budget of 700 million.
Its intention is now to consolidate in these two areas and use these synergies to gain access to the construction and infrastructure branches.
The underground toll track, which will be sponsored by the Office of Infrastructure of the City of Brisbane and will be called Northern Link (northern feeder), has the purpose of connecting the western highway in Toowong with the bypass in Kelvin Grove (see map) over a length of 5 kilometres through tunnels. This is the biggest measure of congestion reduction on the Brisbane roads.
The timetable issued by the city administration envisages the allocation for summer 2010 and the start of the construction work in December next year.
Even if this toll track is already scheduled to open to traffic in the last few months of 2014, it is expected that the construction work will continue until 2016.
The tunnel was designed in 2005.
It has two lanes in every direction, an electronic toll system and a complex venting system.
The Government of Qeland contributes 500 million Australian dollars (308 million euros) to the financing.
For Hochtiep, Brisbane is already a big business.
Austray awards considerable contracts to Hochtief, which yesterday signed a contract with the government of 154 million, again and again.
Through its domestic subsidiary Leighton, the sub-company ACS will improve the infrastructure of the domestic broadband network with fiber optic cables.
This improvement will create fast Internet access for 400,000 people and keep the German company busy for 18 months.
On the other hand, the company has received the construction projection of the 27-storey construction project in the Australian city of Brisbane. The construction work has not yet begun and Hochtief has received 129 million for this.
Also in the United Kingdom, Manchester, Laing O'Rourke competes for the construction and management of two schools to 25 years.
The initial investment amounts to 75 million euros.
FCC receives the contract for a tunnel in Slovenia for 64 million
FCC, through its subsidiary Alpine, has obtained the construction of a tunnel over 2.1 kilometers in length for a highway in Slovenia via the sum of 64.5 million euros.
The company received this contract only a few days after it had been awarded over 130 million for the construction work for the extension of the Bosruck tunnel (Austria).
In this way, Alpine enhances its experience in tunnel construction.
The start of the construction work is planned for the beginning of 2010 and its implementation will drag on over 32 months.
Sra. Rushmore receives advertising budget from Renfe
Renfe has attributed the advertising and marketing services for the next two years to the agency Sra. Rushmore over a sum of approximately three million euros annually, the railway company said.
In this contract there is also the possibility of two extensions of 12 months each. Sra. Rushmore was selected among 16 agencies that presented to this competition advertised by Renfe, 4 of which came into the final round, among them TBWA, which was responsible for advertising in the last three years.
From now on, Sra. Rushmore will be tasked with designing and manufacturing the campaigns.
Penalty over 63 million for France Télécom due to cut off the competition.
The Competition Regulatory Authority in France has imposed France Télécom a penalty of 63 million euros for anti-competitive behaviour in the Caribbean territories belonging to the country.
According to the authority, the telephone provider has restricted competition on landlines and mobile phones by means of the signing of exclusive contracts, pricing plans and loyalty programs for consumers on the verge of regulation.
Together with this sanction, the former French monopoly and still state-owned enterprise has accumulated more than 560 million euros in penalties since 1994 for obstructing its competitors.
The punishment imposed yesterday was even increased, as the authority, which monitors the competition, believes that France Télécom has committed similar violations in the past and has therefore relapsed again.
Application Trading
On the other hand, the subsidiary of the French company has followed the example of other telephone providers and has opened an application trading site on the Internet to increase the revenue from transactions that do not originate from the telephone connection.
In principle, this application website of Orange is active in France and the United Kingdom.
You have to wait until 2010, until this site will also be available to other countries, such as Spain.
The game at the Champions League has earned Madrid and Barça 476.4 million since the start.
The Champions League has become a source of income for football clubs since it emerged in 1992.
So much that Real Madrid and Barcelona have since taken 476.4 million, earning them the third and fifth places of the football clubs that have earned the most money in the league.
The leader of this list is Manchester United.
The leader of this list is Manchester United.
Winning UEFA's Champions League isn't just bringing glory, it's also one of the main sources of revenue from the big clubs.
According to UEFA, the league has distributed up to 5.362.5 million euros to the 105 teams (including 12 Spanish) who have participated in this event since it was founded in 1992/1993.
Real Madrid and F.C. Barcelona have benefited from this distribution.
The white club ranks third in Europe, which has earned the most money through its participation and which, in addition to AC Milan, is the only one that has won the trophy three times.
The reigning Catalan champion and last winner of the former European Cup in 1992 ranks fifth.
The list lead Manchester United and Bayern Munich, two teams, which also took the most money through their participation in the past Champoins League.
Even though they lost to Barça.
On the other hand, Spain is only in the third place of the countries that were able to raise money through the champions, even though it has more titles than all (five, as opposed to four in Italy, three at England and two at Germany).
Distribution
This obvious contradiction is explained by the complicated cash allocation procedure used by UEFA.
In this financial year, the organization, chaired by Michel Platini, expects revenues of 1,090 million from the Champions League.
Of this money, UEFA envisages 413.1 million for fixed payments: each of the 20 football clubs that took part in the qualifying preliminary round (among them the Atlético de Madridad) got 2.1 million.
In addition, those who struggled to participate got 3.8 million through their blossome attendance, in addition to the 550,000 euros for each game they contested.
There's also another bonus for winning (800,000 euros) and for a draw (400,000 per squad). The clubs that have reached the eighth round will each receive three millions; the four who have reached the quarter-finals, 3.3 million.
The last fours get 4 million each.
The winner earns 9 million, as opposed to the second, which receives 5.2 millions.
For example, a football club receives at least 7.1 million and a maximum of 31.2 million in fixed revenues.
Barça, in turn, earned 2.5 million with his victory at the European Supercup in August.
In addition, there are the variable payments, for which 337.8 millions are earmarked.
This money is allocated proportionately to the value of each television market.
The Spanish is one of the first and has 4 allocated places.
Last year's master receives 40% of the allocated money, 30% of the second, 20% of the third-place finishers, and 10% for fourth place.
The other part is distributed depending on the number of games they play at this year’s edition.
Nueva Rumasa offers 61 million for 29.9% stake in Sos
Nueva Rumasa Group leaked details yesterday on the offer to buy shares with which it intends to acquire a cap between 25 and 29.9% of Sos's capital.
A percentage that, due to the number of shares, does not force them to make a public tendering (opa).
In concrete terms, Nueva Rumasa offers 1.5025 euros per share, which are paid out for ten years and with an interest rate of 1% annually due to this postponement.
Yesterday, the Sos shares closed at 1.85 euros, which is why Nueva Rumasa values the company 18% below market value.
According to Nuevan Rumasa, the price of 1.50 euros reflects the real valuation of Sos.
The offer is linked to the appointment of eight of the 15 advisers.
The Jeréz Group gives shareholders a 15-day deadline to share their interest in selling their shares.
CNMV assured that it has not been informed of this offer, although Ruiz Mateos reiterated that it had been in contact with the authority.
With a degree, the deposit would amount to 611.7 million, while the value of Sos would be 254.27 million.
Meanwhile, Sos continues to restructure his management.
In an attempt to remain on the sidelines of possible purchase offers and the judicial quarrels of his ex-managers, the Jesús and Jaime Salazar brothers have announced the appointment of María Luisa Jordá as head of the internal audit.
A decision with which she becomes the first woman to hold a high post at the food company.
It is a newly created post, which is directly subordinated to the chairman of the group.
This is anything but polemic-free because the company is involved in a judicial battle on suspicion of diverting more than 230 million from Sos to other companies in the Salazar family.
It cannot be ruled out that Sos will postpone further capital over the course of the next few months.
With regard to Salazar's credit, ex-advisers Ildefonso Ortega and Ángel Fernández Noriega (CCM and Unicaja representatives) appeared before the National Assembly yesterday, confirming that they had approved the postponement of 212 million without knowing their determination.
CNMV approves Paternina's public invitation to tender for exclusion submitted by investment company Mer
The National Stock Exchange Commission (CNMV) approved the public invitation to tender for Federico Paternina submitted by the investment company Mer last October 9.
The supervisory authority stated that it approved this tender after it had been proven that the conditions comply with the final laws and thus the content of the presented explanatory leaflet can be considered "sufficient".
CNMV has also announced that this offer is aimed at the acquisition of 550,008 shares by Federico Paternina at the price of 7.65 euros per share, which in turn is 8.95% of the share capital, which consists of 6,142,786 euros in shares authorised on the Madrid and Bilbao stock exchanges.
Furthermore, it has also been informed that 5,592,778 million shares have been established which cannot be conferred in any way until the conclusion of the tender and whose price has been determined by Federico Paternina in accordance with the final laws.
New programmes for the assessment of vehicles
In these days of storms and accidents, not only the car workshops deserve
Every day, thousands of vehicles involved in an accident are towed to the workshops, where an appraiser has to assess the damage incurred and the cost of the repair.
Not a single accident is the same and calculating the cost of the parts and working hours can be a lengthy and complicated task.
Calculating the repair costs of between 20,000 and 30,000 euros by hand, including the parts and working hours, can take up to two or three hours.
On the other hand, with the support of the latest computer tools, it is a question of minutes
That’s why almost 100% of appraisers use these types of systems.
The service and application providers for the evaluation of accidents and repairs collect the information they receive from the manufacturers in order to process them afterwards and offer it to their customers in the form of a useful program.
Audatex, part of the American group Solera, is the market leader in Spain; 80% of all reports are prepared with their products.
The other two companies that compete in the tool market for appraising and drafting a report are GtMotive and Eurotax.
Working with the data provided by the manufacturers is anything but simple.
According to Eduardo Velázquez, Audatex's sales manager, work with 63 manufacturers and importers, with each of them providing the information in a different format.
In addition, the amount of data to be processed is increasing, to the point that in the last five years even more versions, variants and engines came on the market than in the entire fifteen years before.
As soon as a new car arrives on the market, the work begins for the companies.
It's a tedious task, because every single of the thousand-thousand-thousand-of-the-man vehicle parts has to be catagolised and its price
In addition, an "intelligent" graphic image is created by each model, on which you can "click" different parts of the vehicle.
If this is a much-sold model, the work can be completed in one week if the procedure proceeds rapidly.
If it is a less common car, it can take up to three or four months. At present, Audatex has 99.2% of the cars sold in Spain with complete information.
Among the more exclusive models, for example, they have information about the Porsche models, but not Ferrari or Lamborghini.
In view of the vehicle park travelling on the road, it is more than 99%.
In order to carry out the documentation work and the production of databases, Audatex has eight (Spania, France, Germany, the USA, Brazil, Mexico, China and Japan) distributed centers worldwide and each of them specializes in certain brands.
The national headquarters are located in Alcobendas (Madrid).
More than a hundred technicians (usually specialists in mechanics) work there simultaneously with three computer screens.
Audatex invests 90 million euros annually in the development of these databases.
Every month they record 2.5 million data and their customers get the updates every other day.
Elaborating this vast flow of information enables companies to use it in different ways, thereby offering different products.
The most common use is the use for the repairs and repairs, but depending on the country there are also tools for the management of scrap parts or to calculate the file or residual value of a car.
The only company that informs about the value of used cars in Spain is Eurotax.
Audatex does not offer this offer in Spain, but in the United States.
When reviewing the products Audatex offers, it’s easy to get an overview of the kind of support it gives industry experts.
This company offers ten different tools, where the star of the AudaPlus products is a standard solution for assessing accidents for appraisers.
It includes vehicles, motorcycles as well as light and heavy industrial vehicles.
Excluding the cost of the parts, it includes the repair times estimated by the manufacturer or the painting prices.
This tool is paided according to the intended use, i.e. for each expert opinion.
It is most expensive for customers who rarely use it a maximum of ten times a month, namely 5.75 euros per month.
On the other hand, every insurance company that prepares thousands of expert opinions negotiates the prize with Audatex.
With other products, such as AudaVIN, you can fully identify a vehicle and the equipment with which it ran from the assembly linehind solely on the basis of the chassis number.
AudaGlass deals with the vehicle windows, and AudaSubastas is an open service for the specialist market on the Internet, with which you can offer for vehicles that have been declared total damage.
Their statistical service is very useful in identifying trends, conducting geodemographic analysis, or obtaining information about the deviations by brand and model.
One can investigate, for example, how many models of a certain car brand had to enter the workshop due to breakdowns or how many of them were involved in a serious accident during a certain period of time.
Gt Motive is the only Spanish company dedicated to the development of these types of computer tools.
It distributes, among others, Gt Estimate, which is also intended for appraisers and in the same way provides digital images, access to parts or prices and official working hours of the manufacturer.
Gt Motive is a company of the Einsa Group, which was founded in 1971 as a provider for services and solutions for assessing damages, breakdowns or maintenance of vehicles.
The GT leader for expert opinions is a reference product on the market.
They work with 24,000 users in workshops, 3,100 appraisers and 53 insurance companies.
Its business volume has risen at 20% annually over the past three years and sales amounted to 10.8 million euros in 2008.
Earlier last year, they began going on the international market with the opening of an office in Paris.
Audatex, on the other hand, was founded in Germany in 1966 and established in Spain in 1979.
According to the company’s sources, 62% of its business is made in Europe and the rest of the world, and the remaining 38% in North and South America. They work with 900 insurance companies and 33,000 workshops, 3,000 of them in Spain.
Total sales in the Solera group (Audatex, Sidexa, Informex ABZ, Hollander and IMS) amount to 557 million dollars, 3.35 more than in 2008.
In Germany, the company has revenues of 19.1 million euros, 7.2% more than in the previous year.
In 2005, Solera Group was worth 1 billion dollars on the stock market and today its shares are traded at a value of 2.4 billion dollars.
Since 2007, they have been on the New York Stock Exchange and part of the Standard & Poor's reference index.
Auction of accident cars on the Internet
Last October, Solera Autoonline Group bought a platform on the Internet for the sale of accident vehicles and motorcycles.
This purchase meant the payment of 59.5 million euros for 85% of the company's capital, which could increase to the remaining 15% next year.
The purpose of this purchase was to offer its customers more services and increase in value, with the possibility of gaining access to a huge international market.
This appraisal and purchase service is aimed exclusively at industry professionals, such as insurance companies, appraisers, car rental companies, workshops, junkyards and car dealers, who must be registered prior to their activities.
This platform was founded in Germany in 19996 and manages more than 650,000 operations throughout Europe, 500,000 of them in Germany alone.
Their main markets are Spain, Greece, Poland and Turkey.
The site has more than 1,500 registered sellers and 4,000 reviewers these days.
Every day 3,000 advertisements are managed and 100 new advertisements are added to the Spanish market every day.
According to Spanish legislation, a vehicle whose chassis number has been deregistered may no longer travel on the roads, but certain non-damaged parts may be used as spare parts.
The cars with historical value, on the other hand, may be registered again, even if they have been deregistered after difficult administrative procedures.
Cost estimate of the workshop in four steps
With the Auda-Taller tool, Audatex ensures that the user receives a cost estimate in just four steps: identification of the vehicle, search of the spare part, creation and preparation of a cost estimate.
Easily handling these systems is a fundamental condition, especially to convince the older professionals, who are usually more or less opposed to the use of these new computer techniques.
The database includes 1,034 vehicles, 666 of which are passenger vehicles, 109 off-road vehicles, 137 motorcycles, 78 vans and 44 trucks.
Of course, you need a computer with an internet connection for use.
After the model to be repaired has been identified on the basis of the chassis number, a graphic of the respective model appears and then the required spare part is selected.
The user can include variables, such as the price for the working hours, surcharges or discounts and thereafter he can have the cost estimate printed and passed on to his customer.
AudaTaller, however, is not a tool for appraisal such as AudaPlus, but rather a reference catalogue.
The main difference between the two systems is that that the workshop does not involve estimated working hours.
The usage costs for this tool are 350 euros a year, an amount that the customer can easily pay.
Audatex is currently working to offer these images in three-dimensional format.
This is an innovation that car mechanics have been waiting for for a long time, as you can choose a door with it, for example, and can then turn the image completely to look at the inside.
